Performance audit — applied changes
Date: 2026-07-20

1. Deduplicated /filters requests
   Files: src/components/ActivitiesContainer/useActivityContainer.ts
          src/components/Reports/ActivitiesReport/useActivitiesReport.ts
   Change: queryKey for fetchAllFilters() unified to ["filters"] in both hooks
           (previously ["filters_search"] and ["reports", "filter-options"]),
           matching src/components/FIlterContainer/useFilterHook.ts. React Query
           now dedupes/caches the three call sites instead of firing 2-3 identical
           GET /filters requests per Activities page load.

2. Memoized activity list handlers + ActivityCard
   Files: src/components/ActivitiesContainer/useActivityContainer.ts
          src/components/ActivityCard/ActivityCard.tsx
   Change: onDelete/onActivate/onPermanentDelete wrapped in useCallback
           (deps: the respective useMutation object). ActivityCard wrapped in
           React.memo. Prevents every rendered activity card from re-rendering
           on unrelated parent state changes (pagination, filters query settling).

3. Memoized user list handler + UsersItems
   Files: src/components/UsersTable/useUsersTableHook.ts
          src/components/UsersItems/UsersItems.tsx
   Change: onSubmit (inactivateUser) wrapped in useCallback (dep: inactivateUser
           mutation object). UsersItems wrapped in React.memo. Same rationale as #2.

4. Replaced useState+useEffect derivation with useMemo
   File: src/components/ActivitiesContainer/useActivityContainer.ts
   Change: filterOptions is now derived directly from filters.data via useMemo
           instead of being synced into local state inside a useEffect, removing
           an extra render pass every time the filters query settles.

5. Memoized DashboardReport chart data
   File: src/components/Reports/DashboardReport/DashboardReport.tsx
   Change: activitiesPerMonth, schedulesPerMonth, expectedRevenuePerMonth, and
           schedulesByFilter (each a .map() over query data) wrapped in useMemo,
           keyed on the corresponding data slice, so they're no longer recomputed
           on every render.

Verification:
- npx eslint on all touched files: 0 errors (2 pre-existing warnings unrelated
  to these changes, confirmed via git stash).
- useCallback dependencies use the full mutation object (not mutation.mutateAsync)
  per the project's Next.js 16 / eslint-config-next react-hooks
  (preserve-manual-memoization / exhaustive-deps) rules.

Not changed (flagged only, no fix applied):
- useSchedulesReport.ts fetches the full unfiltered activity list under its own
  query key for a dropdown, conceptually overlapping with the Activities page's
  paginated/filtered fetch. Different params, so not a strict cache duplicate;
  would need a dedicated lightweight endpoint to fully address.
- Inline eventPropGetter in SchedulesCalendar.tsx and inline items array in
  DashboardNavBar.tsx were left as-is — the components they feed aren't
  memoized and re-render for legitimate reasons regardless, so useCallback/
  useMemo there would add overhead without a measurable win.
